[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2805304193","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2805304193","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2805304193,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nNYuB","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T14:13:30Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T14:15:55Z","body":"Note that while I agree with the core idea, there's no way to opt out of this behavior in this PR. There are some use cases where the decal's opacity should be modulated by the surface opacity, e.g. for blob shadows.\r\n\r\nI suggest adding a boolean property to Decal that controls this behavior (**Override Surface Alpha** defaulting to `false`).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2805304193/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2806411560","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2806411560","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2806411560,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nRnEo","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-15T15:43:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T22:28:06Z","body":"> Note that while I agree with the core idea, there's no way to opt out of this behavior in this PR. There are some use cases where the decal's opacity should be modulated by the surface opacity, e.g. for blob shadows.\r\n> \r\n> I suggest adding a boolean property to Decal that controls this behavior (**Override Surface Alpha** defaulting to `false`).\r\n\r\nAdded! (much more involved than I anticipated)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ecfab890-95b8-473d-b172-a38cb06cf208)\r\n\r\nOne thing I feel is important to note, as I'm no graphics expert, I added padding to maintain the correct buffer size as without it I experienced many graphical issues \r\n```diff\r\nservers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.h\r\n+ uint32_t override_surface_alpha;\r\n+ uint32_t _pad0;\r\n+ uint32_t _pad1;\r\n+ uint32_t _pad2;\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2806411560/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819443919","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2819443919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2819443919,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oDUzP","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T20:30:49Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T20:30:49Z","body":"> One thing I feel is important to note, as I'm no graphics expert, I added padding to maintain the correct buffer size as without it I experienced many graphical issues\r\n\r\nThis looks correct 🙂 We generally name those padding variables without a leading underscore though, i.e. `pad0`, `pad1` and `pad2`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819443919/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819670915","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2819670915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2819670915,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oEMOD","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T23:03:38Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T23:03:38Z","body":"This is likely the most expected behaviour for decals, but I'm wondering if the opposite should be available. That is, lowering the alpha of surface with decals. I can't think of a common use-case, so it's probably not worth pursuing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819670915/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819756122","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2819756122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2819756122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oEhBa","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T00:17:38Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T01:37:07Z","body":"> This is likely the most expected behaviour for decals, but I'm wondering if the opposite should be available. That is, lowering the alpha of surface with decals. I can't think of a common use-case, so it's probably not worth pursuing.\r\n\r\n@Mickeon I was thinking that too, and perhaps an additional toggle ( or dropdown `max, surface, min`) could be added in the future if a good use-case comes up. The closest i've got would be a decal thats fully opaque with a transparent center.  However this would only apply to transparent surfaces to provide a cutout effect. \r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>Example</summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n![New Project](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e556dbe-d03a-49c2-a178-509b58631b5f)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a95b7fd-6dfb-4207-876d-1099b89673f0)\r\n\r\nThese would need to be separate options, since in cases like this, you really don't want the decal to be able to lower the alpha:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ec719d5-bcbc-40cc-8578-7fde0fc709fb)\r\nor to just take the decals alpha\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/940a192d-002f-4279-8684-e9be2c0c7cc0)\r\n\r\nThis is what it could look like if we add a second option to take the min(alpha, decal.albedo.a) instead:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa8f6c5d-035e-480b-883e-ea15ce34c1a4)\r\n\r\nand of course this only works on transparent materials.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nSo, while it's technically possible, I agree it's not generally useful and could be confusing unless there's a clear use-case.\r\n\r\nWith these arguments it makes me wonder if we should change the property to something less powerful sounding like:\r\n`use_alpha_when_greater`\r\n`raise_surface_alpha`\r\n `modify_surface_alpha` \r\n `preserve_decal_opacity` \r\n\r\nsince it doesn't fully override the alpha, merely adds to it if its greater. \r\n\r\nEdit: tomorrow I'll swap this to a dropdown and see how that feels\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819756122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2820467799","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2820467799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2820467799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oHOxX","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T07:49:30Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T07:49:30Z","body":"I like `keep_decal_opacity` personally.\r\n\r\n> Edit: tomorrow I'll swap this to a dropdown and see how that feels\r\n\r\nI would suggest not going ahead with this unless there's noticeable demand. Even then, the property can be replaced into an enum property in the future, if desired.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2820467799/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2820722763","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2820722763","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2820722763,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oINBL","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T09:26:37Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T09:26:37Z","body":"@Mickeon \r\n- changed to `keep_decal_opacity`\r\n- moved shader check above `decal_albedo.a *= fade` (fixes decal being slightly transparent when it shouldn't be)\r\n- updated documentation","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2820722763/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821336930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2821336930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2821336930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oKi9i","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T13:28:28Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T13:29:08Z","body":"> This is likely the most expected behaviour for decals, but I'm wondering if the opposite should be available. That is, lowering the alpha of surface with decals. I can't think of a common use-case, so it's probably not worth pursuing.\r\n\r\nuse cases:\r\n* shooting games: shoot a hole in sth. w/o changing the mesh or its texture(s). IIRC, most people draw to texture to achieve this\r\n* puzzle games (rare case): I saw in a detective series that you can look through frosted glass by putting transparent tape over it. So this feature could interest someone doing puzzles, where they want to hide sth. and then give the player a tool to make sth. transparent in a limited manner.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821336930/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821376373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2821376373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":2821376373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oKsl1","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T13:41:36Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T13:42:24Z","body":"> use cases:\r\n> \r\n>     * shooting games: shoot a hole in sth. w/o changing the mesh. IIRC, most people draw to texture to achieve this\r\n> \r\n>     * puzzle games: I saw in a detective series that you can look through frosted glass by putting transparent tape over it. So this feature could interest someone doing puzzles, where they want to hide sth. and then give the player a tool to make sth. transparent in a limited manner.\r\n\r\n\r\nThose are definitely good use cases. However for the first example this change will only affect transparent surfaces.  It won't allow you to cut a hole in a opaque wall unless that wall is marked as transparent.  The second example is what i was thinking as well in my [example](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-2819756122) where we could cut holes in transparent objects at the least.\r\n\r\nEither way, this may be a case where using a material specific shader on the glass or wall is a better fit than a decal.  Or eventually a stencil cutout.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821376373/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766224681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105416#issuecomment-3766224681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105416","id":3766224681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gfAcp","user":{"login":"yahkr","id":62478788,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDc4Nzg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62478788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr","html_url":"https://github.com/yahkr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahkr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T03:22:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T13:02:14Z","body":"updated to 741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9\r\n\r\nEDIT: a4bbad2ba8a8ecd4e756e49de5c83666f12a9bd5","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766224681/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]